  "result": "Excellent! All 159 tests pass \u2713 (147 original + 12 new). I've successfully added payment terms support:\n\n**src/dates.js:**\n- Added `calculateDueDate(issueDate, terms)` function:\n  - 'NET14': Due 14 days after issue date\n  - 'NET30': Due 30 days after issue date\n  - 'EOM': Due on the last day of issue month (handles leap years correctly)\n  - Returns null for invalid terms\n\n**src/errors.js:**\n- Added `TERMS_INVALID`: Payment terms must be NET14, NET30, or EOM\n\n**src/invoices.js:**\n- Updated `createInvoice()` to:\n  - Accept optional `terms` parameter (defaults to 'NET30')\n  - Validate terms using `calculateDueDate()`\n  - Return `TERMS_INVALID` error for unknown terms\n  - Set `invoice.terms` and `invoice.dueDate` in returned invoice\n\n**Tests (159/159 passing):**\n- 8 new tests in invoices.test.js covering:\n  - Default NET30 terms\n  - NET14, NET30, EOM terms\n  - EOM handling for different months (including leap year)\n  - Invalid terms error\n  - Boundary crossing (month/year transitions)\n\n- 4 new tests in dates.test.js covering:\n  - calculateDueDate with all term types\n  - Leap year handling for EOM\n  - Invalid terms returning null\n  - Month boundary handling\n\nThe implementation ensures:\n- Terms are validated at invoice creation\n- Due dates are correctly calculated for all term types\n- Leap years are properly handled for EOM calculations\n- Invalid terms are rejected with clear error message",
